[ system ]
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Child disposition authoring (private patch R10, spec §11.10.2).

   SNRom_Bridge.AuthorDisposition sends this instead of
   snrom_author_disposition when the NPC IsChild(). Same context JSON
   (npc_name, npc_formid, npc_bio, circle, MARAS flags), same callback
   (OnDispositionAuthored), same labelled-line answer format, but ONLY the
   platonic fields: NAME (echo guard), WHY, LIMIT, ADDRESS. No orientation,
   intimacy, ardor or exclusivity is ever asked: the reply handler leaves those
   unset and R5 forces intimacy to NEVER.

   `[ system ]` must be the FIRST line (markers are load-bearing; see the
   Relationships disposition prompt's header).
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
You are helping describe one specific young person in Skyrim: a child. You describe only friendship, family-like trust and how they treat the people they rely on. Nothing here is romantic or physical in any way, and no answer may suggest it.

RULES
1. Answer for this one child, from what is known of them, not from what their circumstances imply.
2. Two different children must not come out with the same answers.

[ user ]
THE CHILD: **{{ npc_name }}**

{% set npc_uuid = formid_to_uuid(npc_formid) %}
{% set diaries = get_diary_entries(npc_uuid, 5) %}
{% if diaries and length(diaries) > 0 %}
WHAT {{ npc_name }} WRITES WHEN NO ONE IS READING
{% for e in diaries %}
[{{ e.entry_date_str }}] {{ e.content }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

WHAT IS KNOWN ABOUT {{ npc_name }}
{% set profile = render_character_profile("bio_summary", npc_uuid) + render_character_profile("bio_background", npc_uuid) + render_character_profile("bio_personality", npc_uuid) + render_character_profile("bio_aspirations", npc_uuid) + render_character_profile("bio_relationships", npc_uuid) %}
{% if profile and profile != "" %}
{{ profile }}

Any "What You Know About" section above is generated from a counter of interactions, not from what has happened; where it disagrees with anything else, disregard it. Any "Your Bond With" section is this system's own earlier output; do not treat it as evidence.
{% else %}
{{ npc_bio }}
{% endif %}

Answer three things about how {{ npc_name }} holds the people they trust, {{ player.name }} among them. This is about friendship and trust only.

WHY - one short sentence, in third person, on what this child values in someone they trust, and why: what makes them feel safe, what earns their loyalty, what they would do for a friend.

LIMIT - one short sentence, in third person, on a line this child does not cross for anyone, however they are asked: something that comes out of their own circumstances, history or beliefs. Not a rule true of almost anyone.

ADDRESS - how {{ npc_name }} addresses {{ player.name }} when speaking to them: a name, a title or a form of address that fits who this child is and how they see {{ player.name }}. Only a form of address; no endearment that would be odd from a child.

Answer in exactly this form and nothing else:

NAME: {{ npc_name }}
WHY: <one short sentence>
LIMIT: <one short sentence>
ADDRESS: <a form of address>
